    <!-- ===== THE FINAL CHOICE ===== -->
    <section id="final-choice" class="section section-dark">
      <div class="section-stripe-top"></div>
      <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
        <div class="sh">
          <div class="sh-eyebrow">The Core Issue</div>
          <div class="sh-divider"><div class="sh-line"></div><div class="sh-line"></div></div>
          <h2>The Sabbath &mdash; God&rsquo;s Seal vs. Man&rsquo;s Institution</h2>
          <p>The seventh-day Sabbath is the seal of the living God &mdash; the sign between God and His people forever.
          The first-day Sunday is the mark of Rome&rsquo;s authority, exalted above the Word of God.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-radius:1rem;overflow:hidden;position:relative;margin-bottom:28px;">
          <img
            src="/images/the-seventh-day-sabbath-rest-friday-sundown-to-saturday-sundown.jpg"
            alt="The Seventh Day Sabbath Rest — from Friday sundown to Saturday sundown"
            style="width:100%;height:300px;object-fit:cover"
            loading="eager"
          >
          <div style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(to top,rgba(0,0,0,0.7),transparent)"></div>
          <div style="position:absolute;bottom:1.5rem;left:1.5rem;right:1.5rem">
            <h3 class="serif" style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff">The Seventh-Day Sabbath</h3>
            <p style="color:#fcd34d;font-size:.875rem;margin-top:.25rem">A Memorial of Creation &mdash; From Sundown Friday to Sundown Saturday</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qb">
          <p>&ldquo;<em>Remember</em> the sabbath day, to keep it holy. Six days shalt thou labour, and do all thy work: but the seventh day is the sabbath of the <strong>Lord</strong> thy God: in it thou shalt not do any work, thou, nor thy son, nor thy daughter, thy manservant, nor thy maidservant, nor thy cattle, nor thy stranger that is within thy gates: for in six days the <strong>Lord</strong> made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that in them is, and rested the seventh day: wherefore the <strong>Lord</strong> blessed the sabbath day, and hallowed it.&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>&mdash; Exodus 20:8&ndash;11 (KJV) &mdash; The Fourth Commandment</cite>
        </div>

        <!-- SABBATH: GOD'S SEAL -->
        <div style="margin:32px 0;border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.35);border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(28,20,0,0.85),rgba(8,10,32,0.9));">
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0;">
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:transparent;padding:0;">
              <img
                src="/images/the-sabbath-as-gods-seal-name-title-territory.jpg"
                alt="The Sabbath as God's Seal — Name, Title, and Territory"
                style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;"
                loading="eager"
              >
            </div>
            <div style="padding:28px 26px;">
              <div style="font-size:0.74rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.12em;color:var(--gold-soft);margin-bottom:10px;">The Seal of the Living God</div>
              <h3 class="serif" style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;color:#fef3c7;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.2;">The Sabbath: God&rsquo;s Seal</h3>
              <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);font-size:0.92rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:14px;">A seal on a document proves it is real and official &mdash; showing the authority behind it with the official&rsquo;s <strong style="color:#fef3c7;">name</strong>, <strong style="color:#fef3c7;">title</strong>, and <strong style="color:#fef3c7;">territory</strong>. All three appear in the Fourth Commandment:</p>
              <div style="background:rgba(212,165,55,0.09);border-left:3px solid var(--gold);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:14px;font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:0.95rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.9);line-height:1.7;font-style:italic;">
                &ldquo;the sabbath of the <strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);font-style:normal;">Lord</strong> thy God&rdquo; &mdash; <em>His NAME</em><br>
                &ldquo;<strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);font-style:normal;">Lord</strong> made heaven and earth&rdquo; &mdash; <em>His TITLE (Creator)</em><br>
                &ldquo;heaven and earth, the sea, and all that in them is&rdquo; &mdash; <em>His TERRITORY</em>
              </div>
              <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:14px;">At the end of time, those who keep God&rsquo;s commandments &mdash; including the seventh-day Sabbath &mdash; show by their obedience that they are followers of Christ, not of the beast. Revelation calls this the &ldquo;seal&rdquo; on their foreheads.</p>
              <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.2);padding-top:14px;">
                <p style="font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:0.95rem;font-style:italic;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.85);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:6px;">&ldquo;If you love me, you will keep my commandments.&rdquo;</p>
                <div style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold-soft);">Jesus &mdash; John 14:15</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.18);padding:18px 26px;">
            <p style="font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:0.97rem;font-style:italic;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.88);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:8px;">&ldquo;The fourth commandment is the only one of all the ten in which are found both the name and the title of the Lawgiver. It is the only one that shows by whose authority the law is given. Thus it contains the seal of God, affixed to His law as evidence of its authenticity and binding force.&rdquo;</p>
            <div style="font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--gold-soft);font-weight:700;">— Ellen G. White &mdash; <a href="https://m.egwwritings.org/en/book/14809.726" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--gold-soft);text-decoration:underline;font-weight:700;">Read Source &rarr;</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qb qb-dark">
          <p>&ldquo;Sunday is our mark of authority&hellip; The church is above the Bible, and this transference of Sabbath
          observance is proof of that fact.&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>&mdash; Catholic Record of London, Ontario, September 1, 1923</cite>
        </div>

        <div class="qb">
